layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | A
    strong project
    | is a folder you work in with Claude Code on one machine, usually a git repository. Buildyboy creates projects by
    | itself as sessions arrive, and groups everything that happened there: sessions, jobs, cost, commits, pull requests
    | and progress notes. Open
    strong Projects
    | in the top bar (on a phone, go to
    code {{ site.url }}/projects
    | ).

  h2#how How sessions are grouped
  ul
    li
      | A session belongs to the
      strong git repository
      | it runs in (the top folder of the repository), even if you started Claude in a sub-folder.
    li Outside git, the folder Claude was started in is the project.
    li The project's name is the last part of its path, for example shop-api for C:\work\shop-api.
    li
      | The same repository on two machines is two projects, one per machine. This includes Windows and WSL on the same
      | computer.
    li
      | Repositories hosted on github.com are linked to their GitHub page, which is what lets Buildyboy follow pull
      | requests when you add a
      a(href="/docs/settings#github") GitHub token
      | .

  h2#list The project list
  p
    | Each card shows the project's name and total cost, its path and machine, how many sessions it has, its GitHub
    | owner and name, and when it was last active. Click a card to open the project.

  h2#page A project's page
  p Under the header (path, machine, default branch, GitHub link and total cost) you find:
  dl
    dt
      strong Cost over time
    dd Daily cost for the last 60 days.
    dt
      strong Sessions
    dd The most recent sessions, linking to their pages.
    dt
      strong Jobs
    dd Jobs that ran in this project's folder.
    dt
      strong Pull requests
    dd
      | Open and recent pull requests for the project's branches, with their state and checks (
      code success
      | ,
      code failure
      | ,
      code pending
      | or
      code none
      | ). This needs a GitHub token in Settings.
    dt
      strong Commits
    dd Commits made during sessions.
    dt
      strong Recent PROGRESS.md
    dd
      | The latest progress notes written by harness runs (see
      a(href="/docs/composer#harness") the harness prompt
      | ).
  p
    | Projects appear on their own; there is nothing to create or delete. Use the Floor's
    strong All projects
    | filter to see only one project's sessions.
